  "principle": "A primary strength lift may only fall back to something that can still be loaded progressively. Barbell back squat -> goblet squat is a strength session with less load; barbell back squat -> air squat is not a strength session at all, and allowing it would rebuild the exact problem this release exists to fix, one level down. Where no loaded fallback exists the template stays ineligible and the coverage gate says so, which is the honest answer. Bodyweight fallbacks appear only for accessory and core movements, where the stimulus genuinely survives the swap.",
